(WHO and EPA Global Air Quality Guidelines (2024)) Tj T*

(Document ID: REF-AQG-2024) Tj T*
(Source: World Health Organization & US Environmental Protection Agency) Tj T*
(Topic: Air Quality Index Thresholds and Target Exposure Levels) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Key Guidelines:) Tj T*
(1. PM2.5 Annual Target: 5 ug/m3. 24-hour target: 15 ug/m3.) Tj T*
(2. PM10 Annual Target: 15 ug/m3. 24-hour target: 45 ug/m3.) Tj T*
(3. Nitrogen Dioxide \(NO2\) 24-hour target: 25 ug/m3.) Tj T*
(4. Ozone \(O3\) 8-hour peak target: 100 ug/m3.) Tj T*
(5. Sulfur Dioxide \(SO2\) 24-hour target: 40 ug/m3.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(AQI Scale Standard:) Tj T*
(- 0 to 50 \(Good\): Air quality is satisfactory.) Tj T*
(- 51 to 100 \(Moderate\): Acceptable quality for general public.) Tj T*
(- 101 to 150 \(Unhealthy for Sensitive Groups\): Sensitive groups may experience health effects.) Tj T*
(- 151 to 200 \(Unhealthy\): Everyone may begin to experience health effects.) Tj T*
(- 201 to 300 \(Very Unhealthy\): Health alert; risk of severe impacts.) Tj T*
(- 301+ \(Hazardous\): Health warning of emergency conditions.) Tj T*
